  "body": "In #whatwg IRC, it was brought up that the `while` loop examples make it look as though we are locking the browser. This has been expressed previously in private email threads as well. I can easily see the confusion, as that is my gut reaction to such loops too---they look too much like sync-programming busy loops.\n\nWe should make it more explicitly clear that while the API is synchronous for reading data, it is never blocking. And, we should comment the while loops more clearly. They will not lock the browser, but instead will complete a few iterations until the buffer is drained, and then continue onward.\n",
